WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.260
We had pecan trees.

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:07.260
That was our job, to peel pecans. [laughs]

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.380
They were in the yard?

4
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:09.520
They were in the yard.

5
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.520
You couldn't say [laughs] you didn’t have any because you could go get them.

6
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.040
They had a lot of pecan trees out there.

7
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:15.700
There was a lot.

8
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.600
I guess my grandfather had planted them.

9
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.740
We had a lot of pecan trees.

10
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:27.180
My brothers . . . We used to get the pecans young and we would sell them.

11
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:36.420
We'd go out and get the pecans and we'd sit on the side of the road and people stop and buy them.

12
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.500
How much would they fetch usually?

13
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.500
[laughs] Probably not too much.

14
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.120
I don't even remember.

15
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.480
Probably less than a dollar in a little . . . And lot of them was in a little can.

16
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.620
A little thing that we would . . . They would measure them out in.

17
00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:52.860
They would sell them.

18
00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:53.840
We'd sell pecans.

19
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.700
And looked like it was a lot, but I know it wasn't a lot when we would sell pecans.

20
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.940
Bet you thought you were rich.

21
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:08.320
[laughs] We would go to Uncle Ira's store and spend it right away.

22
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.680
Buy some candy or something.

23
00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.200
Selling pecans.

24
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:21.220
You know, I think of Mossville and I think . . . I can't think that I was in the country.

25
00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.140
People say I was raised in the country.

26
00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.620
I know I was raised in the country,

27
00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:35.080
but to me it wasn't raised . . . I wasn't raised where there was truck farms and there was cotton, and there was farming.

28
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:40.460
To me that's the country. [laughs] i guess I thought of us as a little town.

29
00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.160
I don't know what other people think,

30
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:50.460
but I never thought of that as . . . I called the country if you lived down a dirt road and its two or three houses there.

31
00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.760
That would be the country to me.

32
00:01:52.760 --> 00:02:01.800
But let’s see, in Mossville we were on the main road and it was houses all along.

33
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.240
So that's how I saw it.
